From 045acfbd5bbc4aaa833ff9526055d5e7d263daeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wmehanna <wassimmehanna@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:43:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tcg): open the pack early and age it with
 qemu-pcache-compact

- P82_PCOPEN: open the pack on a helper thread, or at machine init
  when an incoming snapshot is loaded (default), cold boots keep the
  lazy open.
- The pack ages itself: per-boot use bitmaps, records stored and never
  hit are dropped after 3 boots, unused for 8 boots after that.
- The exit only writes the use bitmap; the new qemu-pcache-compact tool
  rewrites the pack under its lock (tmp, fdatasync, rename, directory
  fsync), and prints the age table with P89_STAT=1. Lookups compare the
  stored hash before reading a record.
- P89_PACK=legacy and P89_COMPACT_AT=exit keep the old behaviour.
---
